  "kernels": {
    "logicalAllowance": 4096,
    "acquisition": "Repeated fixed-array arguments and temporary slice backing split scalar requests, type/length validation, token work, allocation and INIT. Slice endpoints split omitted defaults, scalar requests, separators, close-token work and completed range acquisition. Named rooted/formal slice capture scans one local row or up to 64 spelling bytes, then separates site allocation, borrow emission and lexical publication.",
    "names": "Argument local/function lookup visits one row or up to 64 spelling bytes. Scoped function lookup retains the existing source_name_work protocol. Array capture and generic reference lookahead use the bounded lookup adapters.",
    "dependencies": "Reference owners use an explicit cursor instead of recursion, preserving the depth-32 limit. Slice selected-parent collapse, retained-owner/ancestor closure, capture lookup, cleanup containment and publication advance one row, IR instruction or dependency edge. Reference CALL preparation scans fresh-site definitions, writes one argument-map byte, then scans retained owners and reverse cleanup rows; publication scans one name row.",
    "children": "Expression/list/group/record/static lowering and record/copy metadata remain named children with their existing protocols. Slice finish requests site construction, checked CALL construction and one-row release explicitly; these legacy leaf builders are outside its scanning bound. No fictitious one-unit bound is assigned to a child.",
    "ownership": "Original mutation/error order is retained. Temporary owners publish before endpoint effects; new views publish after both endpoints. Budget-denied, pending and completed states neither advance work nor replay operations.",
    "adapters": "Private synchronous draining and fixed inline setup remain; no public Pending compiler."
  },
  "covered": [
    "Independent raw acquisition IR/token/capture/error-prefix comparisons for repeated/list/grouped arrays, temporary/named/exclusive slices and invalid endpoint/length/type/IR/register limits",
    "First-match and long-spelling lookup chunks; pending request guards, budget denial, one-operation publication and terminal idempotence",
    "Reference dependency recursion parity including cycles, invalid roots, selected inputs and depth limit",
    "Raw slice finish/publish cleanup-mask and retained-parent parity; reference CALL/release/publish owner retention and partial argument-map/capacity failures",
    "Full-body verifier/VM aggregate CALL/copy/captured scalar regressions and combined CALL depth 32/33 on default stacks",
    "Final owning Engine development/O2 input/output/returned-view/allocator/retention regressions with zero SDK exit heap"
  ],
